        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/t/4da419/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2013-07-30T19:22:53.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>My brother and I were playing a game the other night against Citizen Dawn, and Citizen Autumn was in play. &nbsp;Citizen Autumn, of course, destroys all ongoing cards of the hero with the lowest hp. &nbsp;At one point Bunker and Fanatic were tied with the lowest hp. &nbsp;Bunker had one ongoing card in play, and Fanatic didn't have any in play. &nbsp;We chose to have Citizen Autumn target Fanatic since she didn't have any cards in play thus protecting Bunker's card. &nbsp;Did we play this right? &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I think the main confusion comes from the wording on Citizen Autumn's card. &nbsp;The wording makes it seem as if only one hero is targeted. &nbsp;However, I'm not sure this is the case if two or more heroes have the lowest hp. &nbsp;So, a second question, If two or more heroes have the lowest hp does Citizen Dawn target all of them?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Thanks for the help.</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:38:57.772Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
